---
description: |
  Detects the SOC Prime High-Order Sigma rule "Windows Privilege Escalation &
  Persistence (DetectFlow Attack Chains DEMO)".

  Windows Privilege Escalation & Persistence (DetectFlow Attack Chains DEMO)

  The rule chains 5 stages of SOC Prime behavior rules by host. See
  `socprime::hos::chain` for the correlation and the resulting Detection
  Finding.
args:
  named:
    - name: timeframe
      type: duration
      default: 10min
      description: The time span that a chain must fit into.
    - name: threshold
      type: float
      default: 0.6
      description: The share of stages a host must cover, between 0 and 1.
    - name: tolerance
      type: duration
      default: 1min
      description: How far findings of a host may arrive out of time order.
---

// Generated by scripts/vendor.py from the SOC Prime HoS rule knjkfvZHX16t.
let $stages = {
  seq1: [
    "b479ee8f-e292-4466-95b3-fa000ba3f724", // Explicit COMSPEC Usage in Service File Path (via audit)
    // "0dcdcfa-1709-40fa-bb10-2da285bfe52b", // Missing from the snapshot.
    "780e6396-d9f4-42b2-8d73-89918e2dab16", // Suspicious Service Binary Path (via system)
  ],
  seq2: [
    "c135e89f-a9e5-4cbe-a86c-a25ffa674f1a", // Suspicious Scheduled Task (via audit)
  ],
  seq3: [
    "c170f431-47bc-471f-b539-e73d1135bbf3", // A User was Added to a Admins Local Group (via audit)
  ],
  seq4: [
    "a961fbe5-1acd-49cc-8233-413b46653f52", // Admin Change the Password for other Admin (via audit)
  ],
  seq5: [
    "59a4dcb2-102d-4d23-b6ac-93ffcdba070c", // Windows Security Audit Log Cleared (via audit)
  ],
}
sigma rules=[...$stages.seq1, ...$stages.seq2, ...$stages.seq3, ...$stages.seq4, ...$stages.seq5].map(uid => socprime::$rules[uid])
socprime::hos::chain uid="63c56a0f-afbe-44e8-b83e-814a8daaaf93",
  name="Windows Privilege Escalation & Persistence (DetectFlow Attack Chains DEMO)",
  level="high",
  tags=[
    "attack.t1543.003",
    "attack.t1059.003",
    "attack.t1053.005",
    "attack.t1098",
    "attack.t1070",
    "attack.t1685.005",
  ],
  stages=$stages,
  timeframe=$timeframe,
  threshold=$threshold,
  tolerance=$tolerance
